From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: describe the camera flash

The PM8150L flash block is already described in pm8150l.dtsi but left
disabled, so the handset came up with no flash LED at all and
/sys/class/leds held only the card reader indicator.

Describe the two channels the handset wires to its dual camera flash.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
index 5039a42..a07db8e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/regulator/qcom,rpmh-regulator.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/input/input.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/leds/common.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/media/video-interfaces.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/pinctrl/qcom,pmic-gpio.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/sound/qcom,q6afe.h>
@@ -1326,3 +1327,34 @@ &mdss_dsi0_phy {
 	vdds-supply = <&vreg_l5a_0p875>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * Camera flash. The handset carries the usual dual LED on the two channels of
+ * the PM8150L flash block, which mainline already describes; only the board
+ * side is missing. Currents are kept at the part's conservative per-channel
+ * figures rather than guessed from the stock tree, since the driver clamps to
+ * the hardware maximum and under-driving an LED is harmless.
+ */
+&pm8150l_flash {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	led-0 {
+		function = LED_FUNCTION_FLASH;
+		color = <LED_COLOR_ID_WHITE>;
+		led-sources = <1>;
+		led-max-microamp = <300000>;
+		flash-max-microamp = <1000000>;
+		flash-max-timeout-us = <1280000>;
+		function-enumerator = <0>;
+	};
+
+	led-1 {
+		function = LED_FUNCTION_FLASH;
+		color = <LED_COLOR_ID_WHITE>;
+		led-sources = <2>;
+		led-max-microamp = <300000>;
+		flash-max-microamp = <1000000>;
+		flash-max-timeout-us = <1280000>;
+		function-enumerator = <1>;
+	};
+};
